<!--
# Tables on Durable Objects, under wrangler dev

The document a Worker built from beet serves to prove its tables locally: every
partition of `TABLES` a Durable Object of the one class the Worker exports
(`BeetTableObject`), owning that partition's SQLite storage. Two mounts answer
the table wire protocol, a route reading and writing partitioned tables from
outside the Worker: `/tables` over the objects, `/r2` over a `JsonTableStore`, rows
as json files under `tables/` of the `ARCHIVE` bucket's binding. `/rollup` runs the analytics job against the
objects, archiving cold days into the bucket as SQLite files built inside the
Worker.

Both mounts write without asking who is calling, so this document is for a
local `wrangler dev` alone: beet has no request authentication to put in front
of them yet, and a deployed site must not mount them.

## Usage

Build the Worker, put this document in the local site bucket as `main.bsx`, and
start the dev server with the bindings `examples/infra/cloudflare_workers.bsx`
deploys (`TABLES` bound to `BeetTableObject` with its `new_sqlite_classes`
migration, the `SITE` and `ARCHIVE` buckets, `BEET_REPO=r2://SITE`):

    worker-build --release crates/beet-cli -- --no-default-features --features cloudflare,sqlite
    wrangler r2 object put probe-site/main.bsx --file examples/infra/cloudflare_tables.bsx --local
    wrangler dev --local --port 8787

Then the table suite through the Worker, the row cases over the bucket
binding, and the archive built in the Worker:

    cargo test -p beet_net --features sqlite,server,ureq --lib durable_objects -- --ignored
    cargo test -p beet_net --features sqlite,server,ureq --lib r2_binding -- --ignored
    cargo test -p beet_net --features sqlite,server,ureq --lib archives_in_a_worker -- --ignored
-->
<Router>
	<DurableObjectStore bx:ref="tables" binding="TABLES">
		<ServeTables prefix="tables"/>
	</DurableObjectStore>
	<R2WorkersStore bx:ref="archive" binding="ARCHIVE" {JsonTableStore{path:"tables"}}>
		<ServeTables prefix="r2"/>
	</R2WorkersStore>
	<Route path="rollup" {AnalyticsRollupJob{analytics: $tables, archive: $archive}}/>
</Router>
